{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/997435-solar-awareness-combat-prediction","id":997435,"title":"Solar Awareness: Combat Prediction?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-02T16:48:21-07:00","id":997435,"title":"Solar Awareness: Combat Prediction?","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> I'm in a little bit of a design rut on a new path for solar awareness. As it stands, Solar Awareness is good at three things.<br /> <br /> 1. Anti-Stealth<br /> 2. Join Battle.<br /> 3. Tasting / Hearing / Seeing / Feeling all the things, all at once.<br /> <br /> That's cool, but I'm really only interested in #3 for a character I would like to invest more in Awareness. I was thinking about some other paths awareness could take, and something that came to mind, that I already stunt, is using awareness charms for a character to figure out how their opponent is going to move in combat, or get a few seconds of precognition before something disastrous happens. As far as I can tell, there's no real reason to activate keen sight technique in combat, but I do it anyway for the ~flavour~. <br /> <br /> What if I didn't have to? What if there was a branch of the Solar Awareness charm tree that let the Solar figure out what their opponents are about to do at each step via careful analysis? How could this be made mechanically interesting in a way that isn't &quot;+1 dodge&quot; or &quot;you hit with your sword better&quot;? What types of charms this have? What would you like to see? Any ideas, suggestions, criticisms, or sample charms would be greatly appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T18:39:07-07:00","id":997490,"title":"","content":"I see this branch thematically being very much like the Celerity effects for Brujah and Temporis for the True Brujah in Vamp. Precognition, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11847-kfinigan","name":"KFinigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T18:49:46-07:00","id":997492,"title":"","content":"I view this kind of effect as a prime place to put hybrid Ability Charms. Awareness/Dodge, Awareness/Melee, etc. Prereqs in both trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T18:55:30-07:00","id":997495,"title":"","content":"&quot;Your next line will be 'I'll wipe that cocky grin right off your face.'...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll wipe that cocky grin right off your face!... ah!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T19:32:05-07:00","id":997506,"title":"","content":"The mechanics seem the biggest sticking point here, because precognition of combat actions requires either &quot;rewinding&quot; combat, or forcing people to do things somehow.<br /> <br /> The one thing I can think of is a small tree that improves on and builds off Delaying Actions. There's an initiative cost that could be waved, giving you the choice of acting before other characters in that tick instead of instigating a Clash so there isn't a need to rewind/etc., granting the more boring bonuses in a more flavorful/unique way by having them hinge on how you delay into the action and so on.<br /> <br /> I think that could get some of the flavor of reading your opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T20:22:28-07:00","id":997528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/997435-solar-awareness-combat-prediction?p=997506#post997506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanics seem the biggest sticking point here, because precognition of combat actions requires either &quot;rewinding&quot; combat, or forcing people to do things somehow.<br /> <br /> The one thing I can think of is a small tree that improves on and builds off Delaying Actions. There's an initiative cost that could be waved, giving you the choice of acting before other characters in that tick instead of instigating a Clash so there isn't a need to rewind/etc., granting the more boring bonuses in a more flavorful/unique way by having them hinge on how you delay into the action and so on.<br /> <br /> I think that could get some of the flavor of reading your opponents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, that could be fun, yeah. I've been trying to come up with something that isn't boring, OP, or useless for this sort of thing and that seems like it could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T22:27:31-07:00","id":997556,"title":"","content":"Make a measure oponent charm/tree that tells you your enemy stats if you surpass an appropiate roll.<br /> <br /> Knowing your oponent charms isn't precog, but it can certainly be used to predict what he is going to do.<br /> <br /> Then you can make following charms that give you bonuses if your enemy does what you predicted him to so, similar to that war charm.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12278-broken25","name":"Broken25","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T23:44:28-07:00","id":997577,"title":"","content":"The system transparency the game runs on makes knowing your opponent's stats/Charms (at least ones that you've seen them use) is basically already on the table, Charms would only really have value if you could know things about a character without having seen them do anything yet (which doesn't really seem to be a Solar thing to me, a Sidereal Charm maybe).<br /> <br /> I'd also avoid anything that turns things recorded on a sheet into in-character knowledge beyond abstraction. Having Charms that let you know other character's exact Charms would be useful, but steps all over the line of what's supposed to be stuff that can be known by characters and stuff that's only supposed to be known by players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T00:42:58-07:00","id":997593,"title":"","content":"Maybe make something like that one Lore charm. You say what the next action an opponent will take is. If they do what you said, they get a bonus, if they do something else, a penalty.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T00:52:22-07:00","id":997594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/997435-solar-awareness-combat-prediction?p=997593#post997593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe make something like that one Lore charm. You say what the next action an opponent will take is. If they do what you said, they get a bonus, if they do something else, a penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might work actually.<br /> <br /> Then stick on a Charmtree on top all about being able to target more with it, giving greater bonuses/penalties and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T01:08:37-07:00","id":997598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/997435-solar-awareness-combat-prediction?p=997593#post997593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe make something like that one Lore charm. You say what the next action an opponent will take is. If they do what you said, they get a bonus, if they do something else, a penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Player would just pick sub-optimal actions for their opponents to take, making it a pre-cog ability that fails more often than it succeeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T01:15:41-07:00","id":997600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/997435-solar-awareness-combat-prediction?p=997598#post997598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Player would just pick sub-optimal actions for their opponents to take, making it a pre-cog ability that fails more often than it succeeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that this depends very much on the bonus it gives.<br /> <br /> If the bonus is good enough, I would definitely consider taking the dictated action.<br /> <br /> Though, this then leads us to the problem of the Solar making her enemies stronger unintentionally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T01:38:22-07:00","id":997606,"title":"","content":"I think the problem is that combat is too mechanically strenuous for modelling something after a Lore Charm that's meant to do things like influence military campaigns; which is already a very loose part of the system.<br /> <br /> You'd have to be extremely restrictive on what you can &quot;predict&quot; people will do for a combat Charm. It's not hard to come up with actions nobody would want to take in a fight (&quot;I will kill yourself for daring to raise arms against the Chosen of the Unconquered Sun and die with honor.&quot;) for a mechanical combat bonus, turning it into a debuffer Charm that runs into the concern <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar296_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"296\" data-vbnamecard=\"296\">hippokrene</a> stated.<br /> <br /> Before even getting into bonuses and penalties, there needs to be a thorough consideration of the limitations of the Charm. And then the bonuses/penalties have to somehow be universal and/or varied enough to cover multiple options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T05:05:38-07:00","id":997636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/997435-solar-awareness-combat-prediction?p=997600#post997600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that this depends very much on the bonus it gives.<br /> <br /> If the bonus is good enough, I would definitely consider taking the dictated action.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Melee Dawn Guy, make a Decisive Attack to throw your sword at your Eclipse buddy, incidentally leaving you weaponless. It'll gain ten autosuccesses if you do. If you don't, subtract two off your Defenses.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, that's what PCs <i>will</i> do with this in their hands.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, this was a thing in <i>Scroll of the Monk</i> as well, but at least it was gated behind high Essence and Martial Arts requirements.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:45:12-07:00","id":997725,"title":"","content":"Hey everyone! I'm really loving this feedback, and I'm excited to see people are engaged with this! While I hypothetically like the idea of the player predicting the other character's sheet or what they'll do, my worry is that it'll create a subsystem within the combat subsystem and will significantly slow down the pacing of the game. I think it works well with things like ship combat or the lore charm because those aren't &quot;all hands on deck, entire circle is doing THE THING&quot; time. I'd prefer something less mechanically and extra-layer-y than me personally predicting what this other character would do. More interesting is abstracting that into a set of benefits.<br /> <br /> In that vein, I'm interested in both <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4596\" data-vbnamecard=\"4596\">Ren9077</a> 's idea of having it interact with other trees, like dodge or melee, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> idea of delaying your action for some bonus. I'll write a sample charm for both of these later!. Here's two charm ideas I had that are related to this. They're not eloquently written, balanced (balance wasn't really thought of at all) or filled with fluff: these are merely illustrative of the types of things I was thinking about.<br /> <br /> <b>Battlefield Seeing Fancy Word</b><br /> Cost: ??? Requirements ??? Prerequisite Charms ??? (Instant, Reflexive)<br /> <br /> A rotted tree, a hidden sinkhole, a loose boulder; the solar's acute eye notices all these things. The solar rolls Perception+Awareness as a reflexive action to notice any environmental factors they might use against a difficulty of 4. The story teller creates an environmental hazard which makes sense given this roll; every 2 additional successes on the awareness roll results in an increase of 1 damage die from the environmental hazard.<br /> <br /> <b>Fancy Predictive Use of Your Other Awareness Charms</b><br /> Cost: ??? Requirements ??? Prerequisite Charms ??? (Instant, Reflexive)<br /> <br /> Whenever you are attacked, instead of applying defense, roll Awareness + Essence. Subtract your successes from the attack roll's successes and treat the attack roll's successes as a difficulty for any of your other awareness charms. If you would automatically succeed the check using your ability, then you successfully dodge the attack. If you do not, then treat the remaining successes as roll-over successes.<br /> <br /> This charm does not work if the opponent is using a supernatural method of stealth or suppression which you are using to pass the check; for example, a demon with no smell cannot be noticed with smelling, and a supernaturally silent assassin couldn't be noticed through hearing.\\<br /> *********<br /> <br /> I'm excited to use the idea of delaying your action and dual tree charms too! I'll write some of those up in a few hours <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12025,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","user":"PraxisCat","date":". 11-03-2016, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T09:39:14-07:00","id":997744,"title":"","content":"This might be a bit boring, but what about basing a DV on Wits+Awareness, fluffed as you predicting your opponents attacks and avoiding them with minimum effort?<br /> There's a precedent in using alternative pools for certain actions, such as Devil-Strangling Attitude. It'd make Awareness make more sense as a Dawn caste ability, plus anything that makes Dexterity less of a must-have for everyone sounds like a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T10:38:44-07:00","id":997768,"title":"","content":"I've had to deal with things like this before in other systems.<br /> <br /> First of all, it only really becomes problematic in PvP combat; any situation in which I, the GM, am controlling the opponents means that I can give accurate predictions as to what they're going to do to the players if they have ways of knowing that.<br /> <br /> In PvP, the easiest way of resolving this I've found is to force the player of the character being predicted to lock in their action privately, with me, before moving on to the player of the character doing the predicting. Then I can weigh how much information the mechanical method of prediction will convey through my filter, and give that over. The first player can't do backsies.<br /> <br /> It's always worked relatively well. There have been edge cases, of course. In an Amber DRPG game I had one memorable moment of a character who as a tactical god (which gives you insight into what your opponent is going to do next, but only based on knowledge you actually have) fighting a character who had mentally compromised them and so could read their thoughts as they happened and react accordingly. I had to figure out how and to what extent they cancelled each other out and what information to give both players.<br /> <br /> That's a super edge case, tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T11:41:39-07:00","id":997796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/997435-solar-awareness-combat-prediction?p=997744#post997744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be a bit boring, but what about basing a DV on Wits+Awareness, fluffed as you predicting your opponents attacks and avoiding them with minimum effort?</div> </div> </div> </div>My concern with this is that Wits + Awareness is already super important to combat. Obviously it isn't going to let Awareness replace any offensive Ability, but being able to get a high Join Battle and a high DV out of one Attribute + Ability paring means you have a lot more left to invest into offense since you don't have defense and JB to invest in separately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T14:31:44-07:00","id":997886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/997435-solar-awareness-combat-prediction?p=997796#post997796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My concern with this is that Wits + Awareness is already super important to combat. Obviously it isn't going to let Awareness replace any offensive Ability, but being able to get a high Join Battle and a high DV out of one Attribute + Ability paring means you have a lot more left to invest into offense since you don't have defense and JB to invest in separately.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make it Perception or Intelligence based and not Wits based. Gets rid of the super combo. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12025_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12025\" data-vbnamecard=\"12025\">PraxisCat</a> How about <b>Battlefield Calamity Vision</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 4i, 1wp <b>Requirements: </b>Awareness 4, Essence 3 <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Sensory Acuity Prana (Instant, Reflexive) <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-only<br /> <br /> A rotted tree, a thick bramble, a hidden sinkhole, a crushing boulder; the solar's acute eye notices all these things. With subtle cues that the opponent reads &quot;with ease&quot; she tricks her them into a precarious situation. This charm creates a gambit where the solar rolls their Manipulation + Awareness against the higher of the targets Resolve or Guile. Success tricks the target into maneuvering themselves into an environmental hazard with a base damage of (Essence)L bypassing hardness, lasting 1 round. Successes above the targets defense can be split between additional rounds or increasing the damage by 1L on a one for one bases. The target may take an (Dexterity + Awareness) action, which may not be flurried, against a difficulty of the initiators guile, each success reduces the duration of the effect by 1 round to a minimum of 1 round. <br /> <br /> <b>Keen Predictive Insight Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m, 1wp <b>Requirements:</b> Awareness 3, Essence 2 <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Surprise Anticipation Method (Instant, Reflexive) <b>Keyword</b>: Clash, Withering-only<br /> <br /> Whenever you are attacked, instead of applying defense, roll Dexterity + Awareness. Subtract your successes from the attack roll's successes and treat the attack roll's successes as a difficulty for any of your other awareness charms. If you would automatically succeed the check using your ability, then you successfully dodge the attack. If you do not, then treat the remaining successes as roll-over successes.<br /> <br /> This charm does not work if the opponent is using a supernatural method of stealth or suppression which you are using to pass the check; for example, a demon with no smell cannot be noticed with smelling, and a supernaturally silent assassin couldn't be noticed through hearing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T00:48:48-07:00","id":998640,"title":"","content":"Slightly late to the party - but what about a predictive charm where you (secretly) declare an action you predict the opponent to take on a card (like with the war strategem charms), and if they undertake that action you can a boost - initiative, DV, what have you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/649-nightwinder","name":"Nightwinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T10:08:39-07:00","id":998806,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10131_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10131\" data-vbnamecard=\"10131\">BadassOverlord</a> , I like the idea of using something different than Dex to help with defense; it certainly helps with Dex being the godstat in Exalted! <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12102\" data-vbnamecard=\"12102\">Maudova</a> has the right idea when it comes to helping balance it; if you make it perception / awareness, you get rid of making Wits the new godstat, since it also contributes to resolve and join battle.<br /> <br /> Maudova, good suggestions! I like the thought that went into <b>Battlefield Calamity Vision, </b>but my worry is that it's a quite complex charm. That being said, it's a &quot;free damage&quot; charm, so I don't see why not. As someone who both plays and STs, my general disposition is to avoid as many &quot;check what values each person has&quot; as possible, in order to keep things smooth. That being said, I like the thought that went into this, and it definitely captures the spirit of the act.<br /> <br /> On <b>Keen Predictive Insight Technique</b>, I think the cost is a little high. Ultimately, we want to compare any defense booster to just using an excellency to boost your defense. Assuming you're using keen hearing, we can assume a baseline elimination of 3. If someone's rolling 15 attack dice, let's assume 7 successes. So we need to boost our defense by 3 to get there, assuming we start with a defense of 5. We're at a 2 defense deficit between this charm and base right now. Using just an excellency and a stunt, it costs 4m to get into the &quot;safe zone&quot; and successfully parry. With our dice roll, the results are variable. Assuming we're rolling 10 dice, that's 5 successes. We definitely succeed there. But dice are tricksy, and it could end up being 2 or 3 successes. Then, we're fucked, and we spent an extra 1m, 1wp.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, with an excellency and a stunt, this charm becomes very powerful. I think gating it behind WP is smart, but it might be worth it to gate it behind a battle limit. Maybe &quot;Twice per Scene,&quot; and decreasing the cost from 5m , 1wp to 3m, 1wp.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4596\" data-vbnamecard=\"4596\">Ren9077</a> , here's an idea for an awareness / dodge hybrid charm:<br /> <br /> <b>Battle Ending Intuition</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2m, 1wp <b>Requirements</b>: Awareness 4, Dodge 5, Essence 2, <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Safety Between Heartbeats, Any Keen Sense Charm, <b>Keywords</b>: Uniform, Counterattack, Perilous<br /> <br /> The Solar's senses are deeply attuned to the clamor and chaos around her, and all movements are laid bare before her. Whenever the solar dodges and attack which causes her opponent to lose any initiative, she may make an immediate disarm gambit. She may add any initiative lost by her attacker to make up the cost for this gambit.<br /> <br /> <b>Fool Catching Prana</b><br /> <b>Cost </b>-, <b>Requirements</b>: Awareness 5, Dodge 5, Essence 2. Prerequisite Charm: <b>Battle Ending Intuition. Keywords</b>: Uniform, Counterattack, Perilous<br /> This permanently upgrades the prerequisite, allowing the solar to make any gambit counter attack in response to a successful dodge. Once per scene, unless she successfully dodges 3 attacks in a row.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> , I've been thinking about what sorts of interesting mechanical stuff could be gotten out of delaying actions. I've also thought of breaking up clashes for the Solar's benefit. Here's one for clashes.<br /> <b>Time Stopping Praxis</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m, 1i, <b>Requirements</b>: Awareness 5, Essence 2, <b>Prerequisite</b> <b>Charms</b>: Any Keen Sense, Surprise Anticipation Method, <b>Keyword</b>: Clash<br /> <br /> Whenever a solar would be in a clash, she may instead opt to split the clash into a normal combat action for both members of the clash, and may choose who goes first. If she chooses to go second, she may take a free full defense or a free aim action before her opponent makes their attack.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking about one that combines <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4596\" data-vbnamecard=\"4596\">Ren9077</a> ideas. Here's one that keys off of solar melee.<br /> <br /> <b>Blade Anticipation Method</b><br /> <b>Cost </b>1m, 1i <b>Requirements</b>: Awareness 5, Melee 5, Essence 2, <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Any Two Keen Senses, One Weapon Two Blows, <b>Keyword</b>: Uniform, Perilous<br /> <br /> The Solar marks her target and girds herself, tracing the flow of her enemies hand until it reaches its zenith, misses, and leaves an opening. Upon using this charm, she immediately moves to one tick below her intended target. If she takes no damage from either a decisive or withering attack until her turn, she may activate One Weapon, Two Blows as though she successfully met its requirements, even if she has not.<br /> <br /> At Essence 4+, this charm may repurchased. Repurchasing this charm allows her to chain One Weapon, Two Blows twice if she successfully meets its requirements in the first or second attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12025,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","user":"PraxisCat","date":". 11-05-2016, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:54:36-07:00","id":998924,"title":"","content":"A few charms I came up with based on the idea of predicting your enemy's actions. The problem is neither of this actually call for an Awareness roll, so they don't fit the second requirement of &quot;reason to have all those long-term Charms up&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Stilled Pond Understanding</b><br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Awareness 4, Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One turn<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Surprise Anticipation Method<br /> <br /> The Lawgiver's insight into action and reaction is unparalleled. There are only so many places a person can go, so many actions each person can take. She places herself at the nexus of these choices, reducing them all to one: strike me.<br /> <br /> The Solar selects an enemy within close range when activating this Charm. Until her next turn she may reflexively Defend Other the target of any of his attacks. She may only have one instance of this Charm active at a time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rippling Interference Method</b><br /> Cost: 1m; Mins: Awareness 5, Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Stilled Pond Understanding<br /> <br /> The Solar's foes move as one to strike her down, their planned blows etching out a delicate pattern of bright-edged steel. She moves once, and the pattern turns against itself.<br /> <br /> Whenever the Solar is attacked while suffering an onslaught penalty she may activate this Charm to apply that penalty to her opponent's attack dice pool. She still suffers the penalty as normal unless using other Charms to negate it (which does not interfere with this Charm).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3353-rca","name":"RCa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T13:13:45-08:00","id":999390,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12025_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12025\" data-vbnamecard=\"12025\">PraxisCat</a> on Battlefield Calamity Vision. I thought the upper limit of complexity resided with the grapple rules and so that was my upper level limit on how much brain power someone had to use to process the charm. If you have suggestions on how to smooth it out, I'd love to see them. I wrote a version that just had set values (3 was the old target vs resolve) but it felt like it would cheat someone out of a valid defense. But maybe that's not the worst thing?<br /> <br /> As for KPIT I based the cost off of pre-established clash effects. Except in those effect you commonly performed some counterattack as part of the clash so I thought about lowering the cost there. Then I remembered one of the things you have to keep in mind is that awareness has a scene long dicetrick built into the set (sensory acuity prana) so you get to double 9s on those roles. I'm assuming if your using awareness for some of your defensive advantage you'all be popping that during JB. <br /> Now I would also probably change the wording of the charm, because even though I wrote the structure and pre-requisites I don't actually understand what some of the other text of the charm does. I'll rewrite it to fit with how I think the charm should work when I get to a computer...formatting from a touchpad phone sucks.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":12102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","user":"Maudova","date":". 11-06-2016, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:39:56-08:00","id":999990,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12025_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12025\" data-vbnamecard=\"12025\">PraxisCat</a> How do you feel about this rewrite?<br /> <b>Predictive (Sense) Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m, 1wp <b>Requirements:</b> Awareness 3, Essence 2 <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Surprise Anticipation Method, Keen (Sense) Technique (Instant, Reflexive) <b>Keyword</b>: Clash, decisive-only<br /> <br /> The Solars senses are preternaturally sharped to the point that even the slightest sensory queue forecasts her foes intentions. Whenever she is attacked, instead of applying defense, roll Dexterity + Awareness as a clash action. Compare successes between the attack roll and the awareness roll. If her successes are equal to or greater than her enemies not only is she unharmed by the attack but also allows her to to create a reflexive disengage action against the target, adding her net successes as non-charm dice to the roll. This charm can be used once per combat, reset by returning to base initiative and reaching 11+.<br /> <br /> <b>Special activate rules</b>: This charm does not work if the opponent is using a supernatural method of stealth or suppression which the solar does not overcome with awareness or charms; for example, a demon with no smell cannot be noticed with smelling, and a supernaturally silent assassin couldn't be noticed through hearing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T08:11:15-08:00","id":1004946,"title":"","content":"Sorry about that, I had real life commitments and wasn't focusing on RP stuff.<br /> <br /> I like that, as it allows for a dodge + additional functionality. It wouldn't fit my personal character idea since they're a melee type of person, but this ability is very cool and evocative for a supernaturally talented hunter, for instance. I think adding a reflexive disengage to this, with non-charm dice, really helps justify the 5m, 1wp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T08:22:31-08:00","id":1004951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PraxisCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/997435-solar-awareness-combat-prediction?p=1004946#post1004946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry about that, I had real life commitments and wasn't focusing on RP stuff.<br /> <br /> I like that, as it allows for a dodge + additional functionality. It wouldn't fit my personal character idea since they're a melee type of person, but this ability is very cool and evocative for a supernaturally talented hunter, for instance. I think adding a reflexive disengage to this, with non-charm dice, really helps justify the 5m, 1wp.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could create a reflexive rush instead, allowing them to anticipate any attempt to escape. Pretty easily flipped mechanically and thematically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}